Alternative: give the constructor an option to skip the renderer? That would change the public API used by main.tsx (fine, just adding an option) — hmm, hacky but pragmatic: `constructor(canvas, seed, opts?: { noRenderer?: boolean })`. Actually, cleaner: lazy renderer creation? The frame loop needs it.

Let me check how other world classes are tested in node... the remote-entities tests? Let me check how remote-entities.test.ts works — RemoteEntityLayer probably doesn't need a renderer. And combat-fx? Those tests probably run in node with plain three.js objects.

The simplest, most robust approach respecting the spec's intent:
- Put the lifecycle in a testable class in `self-ship.ts` (create-once, re-tint, rebuild on classId change, dispose on null) — no renderer needed.
